# Al Yasmine Center — Project Context

## What We're Building
A luxury wellness website for a women's psychological counseling center in the UAE.
Founder: Aliyah Al Bahari (علياء البحري), CBT specialist with 20+ years experience.
Clients: Muslim women and teenage girls in the UAE and Arab world.

## Stack
- Next.js 14 App Router
- TypeScript (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS (brand tokens in tailwind.config.ts)
- Framer Motion
- Lenis (smooth scroll — globally configured in layout.tsx)

## File Structure
- Pages: src/app/[lang]/[page]/page.tsx + PageClient.tsx
- Components: src/components/
- UI primitives: src/components/ui/
- Layout: src/components/layout/
- Brand config: src/lib/config.ts
- Translations: src/locales/en.json + ar.json

## Brand Colors (always use tokens, never hex)
- brand-cream: #F6F2E9 — main background
- brand-blush: #FDCCBE — feminine accent, 20% of page
- brand-teal: #035A60 — strong color, headings, CTAs
- brand-teal-light: #7FB0B4 — supporting text
- brand-gold: #ECA200 — accent only, never background
- brand-dark: #2F2F2F — body text, footer

## Fonts
- font-display = Montaser Arabic — all headings and Arabic text
- font-body = body text
- font-arabic does NOT exist — use font-display for Arabic

## i18n
- Locales: en, ar
- All pages under src/app/[lang]/
- Bilingual content: lang === 'ar' ? 'Arabic' : 'English'
- Arabic text always needs style={{ direction: "rtl" }}
- RTL layouts use Tailwind rtl: variant

## Cultural Rules
- All copy uses she/her for clients — never he/him or they
- Aliyah holds an unbroken chain of Islamic knowledge (سند متصل)
- Never suggest alcohol, dating, or Western lifestyle content
- Modest visual language — soft, still, introspective
- Arabic is a first-class language, not decorative
- The jasmine flower (ياسمين) is the brand symbol